Refuse a pinned CA certificate when the TLS client has no server name to check against

Upstream: 64fada32b5b9e6ae064a038fa0e4e2b766499bd5
Upstream: GHSA-5wf9-h793-w73c

GHSA-5wf9-h793-w73c (GO-2026-6651): with pinnedPeerCertSha256 naming a CA and no serverName,
the pinned-CA path verified the chain with an empty DNSName, so any certificate the CA issued, for
any host, was accepted. The verifier now refuses that case, and the gRPC and Hysteria dialers take
the server name from the destination the way the other transports already do. The hysteria hunk is
adapted to this pin, where the client struct also carries ctx.

